  "title": "Retry-based resilience for Windows test fixture cleanup",
  "topic": null,
  "status": "accepted",
  "context": "Test teardown on Windows encounters EPERM errors when removing fixture directories because just-terminated child processes hold file handles briefly. This causes intermittent test flakiness in CI.",
  "decision": "Add `maxRetries: 10, retryDelay: 100` to `rmSync()` calls in test cleanup (9 locations). Document remaining full-suite timeouts in 3 CLI-spawn tests as accepted-risk findings instead of silent flakes.",
  "consequences": [
    "Fixture cleanup tolerates transient Windows handle lag without failing",
    "Test flakiness moves from silent folklore to explicit code visibility",
    "Remaining 3 timeouts (solo green, full-suite only) tracked as accepted-risk findings for monitoring"
  ],
  "alternatives_rejected": [
    "Redesign process termination to guarantee handle release before cleanup",
    "Implement Windows-specific handle-tracking cleanup logic",
    "Continue accepting flakiness without visibility",
    "Skip fixture cleanup entirely"
